<title>USA: Destron Fearing places 650,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Destron Fearing places 650,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Destron Fearing Corp said Friday it completed a private placement of 650,000 shares of common stock at $2 a share with two U.S.-based investors.</p>
<p>The private placement raised $1.3 million in equity financing, the company said.  </p>
<p>Earlier this week, Destron Fearing said it placed $2 million in common stock with three foreign institutions.</p>
<p>&quot;The financing announced today completes our present 1997 equity financing plan and should assure us of adequate working capital to meet our requirements,&quot; said Randolph Geissler, president and chief executive.</p>
<p>Destron Fearing manufactures electronic and visual identification devices for animals.</p>
<p>Shares of Destron traded up 1/16 at 3-1/16.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
